+| Failure | What happens |
+| --- | --- |
+| 429 on a key | That key is benched for 60 s (or its `Retry-After`) and the next key tries the same model |
+| 401/403 on a key | That key is benched for an hour and the next key tries the same model |
+| Every key rate limited | Shift down to the next model |
+| Every key rejected | Fail fast — a bad key fails identically on every model |
+| 404/408/5xx, connection or timeout | Shift down to the next model on the same key — other keys share the model's capacity |
+| 400 | Fail fast — a bad request fails identically everywhere |
+
+The pool is sticky: whichever key last succeeded is tried first next time. A
+benched key goes to the back of the order rather than being skipped, so a pool
+where every key is cooling still makes one last attempt. Logs name keys by
+position (`key #2`), never by value. A malformed *plan* does not shift either:
+that is a planning failure, not an availability one. If every rung fails,
+`PlannerAPIError` lists each attempt.
 
